{"data": [{"paperId": "17ea720763cc8e7274eb694f33df7a55171dcc1c", "title": "Deep Compact Polyhedral Conic Classifier for Open and Closed Set Recognition", "year": 2021, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.12570", "status": "GREEN", "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.12570, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2277308", "name": "Hakan Cevikalp"}, {"authorId": "152438412", "name": "Bedirhan Uzun"}, {"authorId": "1976000468", "name": "Okan Kopuklu"}, {"authorId": "1908321", "name": "Gurkan Ozturk"}], "abstract": "Abstract In this paper, we propose a new deep neural network classifier that simultaneously maximizes the inter-class separation and minimizes the intra-class variation by using the polyhedral conic classification function. The proposed method has one loss term that allows the margin maximization to maximize the inter-class separation and another loss term that controls the compactness of the class acceptance regions. Our proposed method has a nice geometric interpretation using polyhedral conic function geometry. We tested the proposed method on various visual classification problems including closed/open set recognition and anomaly detection. The experimental results show that the proposed method typically outperforms other state-of-the-art methods, and becomes a better choice compared to other tested methods especially for open set recognition type problems. The source code of the proposed method is available at https://github.com/bdrhn9/dc-epcc .", "matchScore": 302.60437}]}
